<Row><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Live CMS</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">bxmRPYRgQA99Uzyis6dO</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">night-skincare-routine</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Night Skincare Routine</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1782128191225</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">content-full</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">What Happens to Your Skin While You Sleep?
During sleep, the skin naturally focuses on renewal and maintenance.
This is why nighttime skincare often emphasizes:
? Hydration
? Nourishment
? Skin barrier support
? Moisture retention
Providing your skin with proper care before bed helps support these natural processes.
Step 1: Remove Makeup and Surface Impurities
If you wear makeup or sunscreen, proper removal is essential.
Why It Matters
Sleeping with makeup can lead to:
Product buildup

Dull appearance

Uneven texture

Start by thoroughly removing:
? Makeup
? Sunscreen
? Dirt
? Excess oil
This prepares the skin for cleansing.
Step 2: Cleanse Your Skin
A cleanser removes remaining impurities from the skin&apos;s surface.
Benefits
? Fresh feeling skin
? Cleaner complexion
? Better product absorption
? Reduced buildup
Choose a gentle cleanser suitable for your skin type.
How to Cleanse Properly
Wet your face with lukewarm water.

Apply cleanser.

Massage gently.

Rinse thoroughly.

Pat dry.

Avoid harsh scrubbing.
Step 3: Apply Toner
Toners help prepare the skin for serums and moisturizers.
Benefits
? Refreshes the skin
? Supports hydration
? Improves product layering
? Enhances skincare experience
Hydrating toners are particularly useful in nighttime routines.
Step 4: Apply Hyaluronic Acid Serum
Hydration is one of the most important aspects of nighttime skincare.
Why Use Hyaluronic Acid Serum?
Hyaluronic Acid helps support moisture retention.
Benefits
? Deep hydration
? Plumper-looking skin
? Improved smoothness
? Enhanced glow
? Better skin comfort
Apply a few drops evenly across the face and neck.
Step 5: Apply Collagen Serum
Collagen Serum complements hydration-focused routines.
Benefits
? Supports skin appearance
? Helps maintain smooth texture
? Promotes healthy-looking skin
? Complements anti-aging skincare routines
Many users combine Hyaluronic Acid Serum and Collagen Serum at night.
Why Hyaluronic Acid and Collagen Work Well Together
Hyaluronic Acid
Focuses on hydration.
Collagen Serum
Supports skin appearance and firmness-focused routines.
Together they help create a comprehensive overnight skincare routine.
Step 6: Apply Moisturizer
