<Row><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Live CMS</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">sNqPx95Vp6jJl6v2gi7E</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">collagen-serum-benefits-complete-guide-for-firmer-youthful-looking-skin</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Collagen Serum Benefits: Complete Guide for Firmer, Youthful-Looking Skin</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1782121902638.9531</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">content-full</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">What is Collagen?
Collagen is the most abundant protein in the human body.
It helps provide structure to:
Skin

Hair

Nails

Bones

Connective tissues

In the skin, collagen contributes to:
? Firmness
? Elasticity
? Smooth texture
? Youthful appearance
As collagen levels decrease with age, skin may begin to show visible signs of aging.
Why Does Collagen Decline?
Several factors can affect collagen production.
Aging
Natural collagen production slows over time.
Sun Exposure
Excessive UV exposure may affect skin structure.
Pollution
Environmental stressors can impact skin health.
Poor Lifestyle Habits
Smoking

Lack of sleep

Poor nutrition

may contribute to premature skin aging.</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell></Row>
