<Row><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Live CMS</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Xq3AmluhcWYoMq7uMjjH</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">best-serum-for-dry-skin-complete-guide-to-hydrated-healthy-glowing-skin</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Best Serum for Dry Skin: Complete Guide to Hydrated, Healthy &amp; Glowing Skin</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1782114734392</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">content-full</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">What Causes Dry Skin?
Understanding the cause of dry skin helps you choose the right products.
Common causes include:
Weather Changes
Cold temperatures and low humidity can reduce moisture levels.
Hot Showers
Excessively hot water may strip natural oils from the skin.
Harsh Cleansers
Strong cleansing products can weaken the skin barrier.
Aging
As we age, skin naturally produces less oil.
Dehydration
Not drinking enough water can affect overall skin hydration.
Environmental Factors
Pollution, air conditioning, and sun exposure may contribute to dryness.
Signs You Have Dry Skin
Common symptoms include:
? Tightness
? Flakiness
? Rough texture
? Dull appearance
? Increased sensitivity
? Lack of natural glow
If these symptoms occur regularly, your skin may benefit from a hydration-focused routine.
Why Serums Are Important for Dry Skin
Unlike traditional creams, serums contain concentrated active ingredients that penetrate the skin more efficiently.
Benefits include:
? Deep hydration
? Lightweight texture
? Improved absorption
? Better skin comfort
? Enhanced glow
Serums work best when combined with moisturizers.</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell></Row>
