<Row><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Live CMS</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">AubG41A0124kcUX1SOkn</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">airwrap-hair-styler-guide-how-to-use-an-airwrap-for-perfect-hairstyles</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Airwrap Hair Styler Guide | How to Use an Airwrap for Perfect Hairstyles</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">4</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1782109682227.5325</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">image-content</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Preparing Hair Before Styling
Preparation is important for achieving better results.
Step 1: Wash Hair
Start with clean hair.
Use:
? Mild shampoo
? Conditioner
Clean hair styles more effectively.
Step 2: Apply Hair Serum
A lightweight serum helps:
? Improve smoothness
? Reduce frizz
? Enhance shine
Step 3: Dry Hair Slightly
Most Airwrap styles work best on damp hair rather than soaking wet hair.
Hair should be approximately:
70�80% dry
before styling. How to Create Curls with an Airwrap
Step 1
Attach the curling barrel.
Step 2
Section the hair.
Step 3
Bring a small section near the barrel.
Step 4
Allow the airflow to wrap the hair around the barrel.
Step 5
Hold for several seconds.
Step 6
Release gently.
Step 7
Repeat throughout the hair.
This technique helps create soft, defined curls.</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/ilika-1de91.firebasestorage.app/o/blogs%2Fsections%2F1782109711304_ilika-airwrap-multi-styler-kit-5-in-1-hair-styling-tool-for-curling-straightening-volumizing-drying-variant-images-1.webp?alt=media&amp;token=ad2271f9-efce-48d4-9eec-4a0933c7be1d</Data></Cell></Row>
