Frequently Asked Questions
What is CTM in skincare?
CTM stands for Cleanser, Toner, and Moisturizer.
Is CTM necessary every day?
Yes. Daily CTM helps maintain healthy-looking skin.
Can I add serum to my CTM routine?
Yes. Hyaluronic Acid Serum and Collagen Serum fit perfectly into a CTM routine.
Should oily skin use moisturizer?
Absolutely. Hydration is important for all skin types.
What comes first: toner or moisturizer?
Toner always comes before moisturizer.
Conclusion
A CTM routine remains one of the most effective and beginner-friendly ways to maintain healthy, hydrated, and glowing skin. By consistently cleansing, toning, and moisturizing, you create a strong foundation that supports all other skincare products and treatments.
Whether your skin is dry, oily, combination, or sensitive, the right CTM routine can help improve skin comfort, appearance, and long-term health.</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String"></Data></Cell></Row>
<Row><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Live CMS</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">siESfVOCOLmzbUX9D5nD</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">hydra-gel-moisturizer-benefits-why-lightweight-hydration-is-essential-for-healthy-skin</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Hydra Gel Moisturizer Benefits: Why Lightweight Hydration Is Essential for Healthy Skin</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">1</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">main-content</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">content</Data></Cell><Cell><Data ss:Type="String">Write Ilika Hydra Gel Moisturizer Benefits
